    "site_desc": "Estero El Sargento (ES, 29.34°N, -112.28°W) is a coastal lagoon located within the lagoon system of Canal del Infiernillo y Esteros del Territorio Comcáac  established as a RAMSAR protected area (site number 1891) in 2009. The tree species at the site are red (Rhizophora mangle), white (Laguncularia racemosa), and black (Avicennia germinans) mangroves reaching an average height canopy of 4 meters. The mean diameter at breast height of trees is 8.01±0.24 cm, with a density of 3960 trees ha-1, and a basal area of 38.24±5.7 m2 ha-1",
